cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or publish results produced with it, please cite it as below."
title: "CAG Bench: Benchmarking Context Accumulation Generation for Long-Running AI Workflows"
authors:
  - family-names: "Canfield"
    given-names: "Seth"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-05-01"
license: "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
repository-code: "https://github.com/GuideboardLabs/cag-bench"
url: "https://github.com/GuideboardLabs/cag-bench"
abstract: >-
  CAG Bench is a benchmark suite for comparing RAG, DAG, and CAG
  approaches on long-running iterative project workflows. CAG, or Context
  Accumulation Generation, tests whether durable project context accumulated
  across sequential tasks improves continuity, reduces contradiction, and
  supports better late-stage project outputs.
keywords:
  - "CAG"
  - "Context Accumulation Generation"
  - "RAG"
  - "DAG"
  - "AI agents"
  - "benchmark"
  - "project memory"
  - "local models"
